(2249580, 309888, 49578, '<td valign="top">very sweet</td>', 'very sweet', '2006-03-22 22:39:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(2249582, 308414, 49578, '<td valign="top">The snap is nice, but frankly i could not relate to the title. Not that the title affects my rating!</td>', 'The snap is nice, but frankly i could not relate to the title. Not that the title affects my rating!', '2006-03-22 22:40:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(2249583, 309449, 49578, '<td valign="top">I love the framing and the composition and the red green and neutral colour arrangement. What bothers me is the hot spot seen from in between the hands. There''s almost nothing except white there. Also a little more DoF could have helped.</td>', 'I love the framing and the composition and the red green and neutral colour arrangement. What bothers me is the hot spot seen from in between the hands. There''s almost nothing except white there. Also a little more DoF could have helped.', '2006-03-22 22:42:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(2249590, 309214, 49865, '<td valign="top">nice idea with this. a qualm i have with it though is that it''s pretty apparent the paint wasn''t dry, at least on the yellow hand, especially around the thumb where a lot of light is being reflected and creating a distraction that draws attention. my last point is obviously personal opinion, and i''m sure people would disagree with me here, but i think more thought could have been given to the placement of th ehands. maybe if they were aligned each 120 degrees to one another to form spokes of a wheel, although i admit that''s probably a bit cliche. the issue for me is that the blue hand kind of disappears behind the other colors, which could be helped either with my first suggestion, using a white background to increase contrast between the background and blue hand, OR move the blue hand towards the top because the yellow hand is bright enough to stand out against the black background. just some thoughts. -6-</td>', 'nice idea with this. a qualm i have with it though is that it''s pretty apparent the paint wasn''t dry, at least on the yellow hand, especially around the thumb where a lot of light is being reflected and creating a distraction that draws attention. my last point is obviously personal opinion, and i''m sure people would disagree with me here, but i think more thought could have been given to the placement of th ehands. maybe if they were aligned each 120 degrees to one another to form spokes of a wheel, although i admit that''s probably a bit cliche. the issue for me is that the blue hand kind of disappears behind the other colors, which could be helped either with my first suggestion, using a white background to increase contrast between the background and blue hand, OR move the blue hand towards the top because the yellow hand is bright enough to stand out against the black background. just some thoughts. -6-', '2006-03-22 22:44:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(2249595, 308057, 49865, '<td valign="top">i like the very clear circularity/linking on this one, very good job.</td>', 'i like the very clear circularity/linking on this one, very good job.', '2006-03-22 22:46:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(2249607, 309545, 41574, '<td valign="top">I like the movement that''s been captured; it greatly emphasizes the importance of the hands, and makes the shot make sense. That said, it''s not, by any means, a great picture. So, cool concept, creative execution, mediocre "technicals"..."5."</td>', 'I like the movement that''s been captured; it greatly emphasizes the importance of the hands, and makes the shot make sense. That said, it''s not, by any means, a great picture. So, cool concept, creative execution, mediocre "technicals"..."5."', '2006-03-22 22:50:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(2249610, 308429, 41574, '<td valign="top">Aawww, too bad the bottom left isn''t in sharp focus; it''s having been so could have improved an already-great shot.</td>', 'Aawww, too bad the bottom left isn''t in sharp focus; it''s having been so could have improved an already-great shot.', '2006-03-22 22:50:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(2249611, 309872, 41574, '<td valign="top">Nice idea; mediocre shot.</td>', 'Nice idea; mediocre shot.', '2006-03-22 22:51:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(2249614, 307909, 41574, '<td valign="top">Too bad the face, and not the hands, seems to be the focus of the shot.</td>', 'Too bad the face, and not the hands, seems to be the focus of the shot.', '2006-03-22 22:51:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(2249617, 307436, 41574, '<td valign="top">Whoa...massive fingerprints.</td>', 'Whoa...massive fingerprints.', '2006-03-22 22:52:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(2249622, 309383, 41574, '<td valign="top">As far as the subject is concerned, it''s just a simple shot of a hand with a ring on each finger: it gets the job done, but isn''t terribly creative or interesting. Technically, the flash kills the shot. <i>Everything</i> is horrifically over-exposed and "flat." Better luck next time.</td>', 'As far as the subject is concerned, it''s just a simple shot of a hand with a ring on each finger: it gets the job done, but isn''t terribly creative or interesting. Technically, the flash kills the shot. Everything is horrifically over-exposed and "flat." Better luck next time.', '2006-03-22 22:54:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(2249625, 309559, 41574, '<td valign="top">Good shot, but your focus goes out towards the bottom of the subject. A narrower aperture might have helped.</td>', 'Good shot, but your focus goes out towards the bottom of the subject. A narrower aperture might have helped.', '2006-03-22 22:54:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(2249630, 307330, 41574, '<td valign="top">The window/door at the left of the frame seems like an over-looked error, as it distracts from the shot. Also, the "clever" part of the picture (i.e., the hand, itself), is abruptly cut out of the frame.</td>', 'The window/door at the left of the frame seems like an over-looked error, as it distracts from the shot. Also, the "clever" part of the picture (i.e., the hand, itself), is abruptly cut out of the frame.', '2006-03-22 22:56:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(2249634, 307193, 41574, '<td valign="top">Unless doing so happens to serve some sort of artistic end, <b>never</b> include a timestamp in a submission; it just looks tacky (though, to your credit, yours blends in well with the image). Other than that little "advice," I''ll say that I like the shot; it''s "OK."</td>', 'Unless doing so happens to serve some sort of artistic end, never include a timestamp in a submission; it just looks tacky (though, to your credit, yours blends in well with the image). Other than that little "advice," I''ll say that I like the shot; it''s "OK."', '2006-03-22 22:57:34.000000', NULL, 1),
